{"id":"5609e5894b943af5","group":"58","path":"58/batch20/58-thm-chebotarev.md","title":"Chebotarev Density Theorem","display":"thm-chebotarev — Chebotarev Density Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-chebotarev","aliases":["58-thm-chebotarev"],"display":"thm-chebotarev — Chebotarev Density Theorem","depends_on":["[[58-df-galois-group]]","[[58-df-field-extension]]","[[../batch17/58-df-dirichlet-density.md]]","[[58-df-equinumerous]]","[[../batch01/58-df-ivc.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-chebotarev"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-chebotarev</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-chebotarev — Chebotarev Density Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"dac0596ff0a0af4a\" href=\"?note=dac0596ff0a0af4a\" title=\"58-df-galois-group\">58-df-galois-group</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"699918fd54cc2a8e\" href=\"?note=699918fd54cc2a8e\" title=\"58-df-field-extension\">58-df-field-extension</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"8acc7c3954935c64\" href=\"?note=8acc7c3954935c64\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-dirichlet-density.md\">../batch17/58-df-dirichlet-density.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"28c79fde9f892bfe\" href=\"?note=28c79fde9f892bfe\" title=\"58-df-equinumerous\">58-df-equinumerous</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"37336284b6cfdfa6\" href=\"?note=37336284b6cfdfa6\" title=\"../batch01/58-df-ivc.md\">../batch01/58-df-ivc.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"K,L,G,C,S_C\\in V\">\\(K,L,G,C,S_C\\in V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"m,n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\">\\(m,n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NumberField}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{NumberField}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NormalExtension}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{NormalExtension}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SeparableExtension}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{SeparableExtension}_S\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{FieldExtension}_S(L,K)\">\\(\\mathrm{FieldExtension}_S(L,K)\\)</span> specify a finite Galois extension of number fields.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Gal}_S(G,L,K)\">\\(\\mathrm{Gal}_S(G,L,K)\\)</span> is the Galois-group predicate, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"C=\\{hgh^{-1}:h\\in G\\}\">\\(C=\\{hgh^{-1}:h\\in G\\}\\)</span> for some <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"g\\in G\">\\(g\\in G\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal P_K\">\\(\\mathcal P_K\\)</span> is the nonzero prime-ideal set from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"8acc7c3954935c64\" href=\"?note=8acc7c3954935c64\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-dirichlet-density.md\">../batch17/58-df-dirichlet-density.md</a>; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{UnramifiedPrime}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{UnramifiedPrime}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{FrobeniusClass}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{FrobeniusClass}_S\\)</span> type the Frobenius data.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NaturalPrimeDensity}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{NaturalPrimeDensity}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DirichletDensity}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{DirichletDensity}_S\\)</span> are the exact density relations.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S\\)</span> is the exact cardinality-comparison predicate.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}chebotarev}\\vdash \\mathrm{NumberField}_S(K)\\land\\mathrm{NumberField}_S(L)\\land\\mathrm{FieldExtension}_S(L,K)\\land[L:K]\\in\\omega\\land\\mathrm{NormalExtension}_S(L,K)\\land\\mathrm{SeparableExtension}_S(L,K)\\land\\mathrm{Gal}_S(G,L,K)\\land\\exists g\\in G\\;(C=\\{hgh^{-1}:h\\in G\\})\\land S_C=\\{\\mathfrak p\\in\\mathcal P_K:\\mathrm{UnramifiedPrime}_S(\\mathfrak p,L,K)\\land\\mathrm{FrobeniusClass}_S(C,\\mathfrak p,L,K)\\}\\to\\exists m,n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S(C,m)\\land\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S(G,n)\\land\\mathrm{NaturalPrimeDensity}_S\\!\\left(S_C,K,\\frac{m}{n}\\right)\\land\\mathrm{DirichletDensity}_S\\!\\left(S_C,K,\\frac{m}{n}\\right)\\Bigr).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}chebotarev}\\vdash \\mathrm{NumberField}_S(K)\\land\\mathrm{NumberField}_S(L)\\land\\mathrm{FieldExtension}_S(L,K)\\land[L:K]\\in\\omega\\land\\mathrm{NormalExtension}_S(L,K)\\land\\mathrm{SeparableExtension}_S(L,K)\\land\\mathrm{Gal}_S(G,L,K)\\land\\exists g\\in G\\;(C=\\{hgh^{-1}:h\\in G\\})\\land S_C=\\{\\mathfrak p\\in\\mathcal P_K:\\mathrm{UnramifiedPrime}_S(\\mathfrak p,L,K)\\land\\mathrm{FrobeniusClass}_S(C,\\mathfrak p,L,K)\\}\\to\\exists m,n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S(C,m)\\land\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S(G,n)\\land\\mathrm{NaturalPrimeDensity}_S\\!\\left(S_C,K,\\frac{m}{n}\\right)\\land\\mathrm{DirichletDensity}_S\\!\\left(S_C,K,\\frac{m}{n}\\right)\\Bigr).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Both density notions are stated through registered relations.  The finite numerator and denominator are witnessed by equinumerosity, so the density value no longer relies on unsourced cardinality bars or division of cardinals.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-galois-group","status":"resolved","id":"dac0596ff0a0af4a","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-galois-group]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-field-extension","status":"resolved","id":"699918fd54cc2a8e","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-field-extension]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-dirichlet-density.md","status":"resolved","id":"8acc7c3954935c64","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-df-dirichlet-density.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-equinumerous","status":"resolved","id":"28c79fde9f892bfe","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-equinumerous]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch01/58-df-ivc.md","status":"resolved","id":"37336284b6cfdfa6","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch01/58-df-ivc.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-dirichlet-density.md","status":"resolved","id":"8acc7c3954935c64","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathcal P_K$ is the nonzero prime-ideal set from [[../batch17/58-df-dirichlet-density.md]]; $\\mathrm{UnramifiedPrime}_S$ and $\\mathrm{FrobeniusClass}_S$ type the Frobenius data.","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"K,L,G,C,S_C\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"m,n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{NumberField}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{NormalExtension}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SeparableExtension}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{FieldExtension}_S(L,K)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Gal}_S(G,L,K)","display":false},{"tex":"C=\\{hgh^{-1}:h\\in G\\}","display":false},{"tex":"g\\in G","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal P_K","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{UnramifiedPrime}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{FrobeniusClass}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{NaturalPrimeDensity}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{DirichletDensity}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}chebotarev}\\vdash \\mathrm{NumberField}_S(K)\\land\\mathrm{NumberField}_S(L)\\land\\mathrm{FieldExtension}_S(L,K)\\land[L:K]\\in\\omega\\land\\mathrm{NormalExtension}_S(L,K)\\land\\mathrm{SeparableExtension}_S(L,K)\\land\\mathrm{Gal}_S(G,L,K)\\land\\exists g\\in G\\;(C=\\{hgh^{-1}:h\\in G\\})\\land S_C=\\{\\mathfrak p\\in\\mathcal P_K:\\mathrm{UnramifiedPrime}_S(\\mathfrak p,L,K)\\land\\mathrm{FrobeniusClass}_S(C,\\mathfrak p,L,K)\\}\\to\\exists m,n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S(C,m)\\land\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S(G,n)\\land\\mathrm{NaturalPrimeDensity}_S\\!\\left(S_C,K,\\frac{m}{n}\\right)\\land\\mathrm{DirichletDensity}_S\\!\\left(S_C,K,\\frac{m}{n}\\right)\\Bigr).","display":true}],"bytes":2047,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4074","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch20/58-thm-chebotarev.md|58-thm-chebotarev]]（batch20）"}],"outgoing":["dac0596ff0a0af4a","699918fd54cc2a8e","8acc7c3954935c64","28c79fde9f892bfe","37336284b6cfdfa6"]}